[31m-# ResearchHub[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A research collaboration platform focusing on regional issues, bridging academia between Central Asian and European Union universities[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 🌍 Overview[m
[31m-This platform bridges academia by enabling:[m
[31m-- Professors to post research topics, details, and student requirements[m
[31m-- Students to apply and schedule interviews through the platform[m
[31m-- Rankings of universities and professors based on platform activity and engagement[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 🚀 Features[m
[31m-- Professor profiles & research topic listings[m
[31m-- Student profiles & application system[m
[31m-- Interview scheduling interface[m
[31m-- University & professor activity-based rankings[m
[31m-- Admin interface for moderation & stats[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 🧱 Tech Stack[m
[31m-- **Frontend**: React, Next.js, TailwindCSS[m
[31m-- **Backend**: Node.js (API routes), possibly integrated with a NoSQL/SQL DB[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 📁 Folder Structure[m
[31m-├── frontend/ # Frontend source code (pages, components, styles)[m
[31m-├── backend/ # Backend routes (API handlers, DB logic, auth)[m
[31m-├── .gitignore # Ignored files and folders for Git[m
[31m-└── README.md # Project documentation[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## 📦 Usage[m
[31m-[m
[31m-You can build and run the entire platform using Docker Compose.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-> [!IMPORTANT][m
[31m-> Make sure to run all Docker commands **from the root folder** of the project  [m
[31m-> (the folder containing `compose.yaml`).[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Requirements[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- You must have Docker installed[m
[31m-- For windows users - you must use WSL2[m
[31m-- You must also create an `.env` file [m
[31m-[m
[31m-The `.env` file's contents must be like so:[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-DB_USER=admin[m
[31m-DB_PASSWORD=password[m
[31m-JWT_SECRET=SecretJwtKeyThatIsAtLeast32BytesLongInBase64[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-When running locally the user and password don't matter, but in production, a secret password will be used, which must not be leaked.[m
[31m-When deploying to production, the JWT secret must be generated using the following command:[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-openssl rand -base64 32[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Build, Run and Stop the project[m
[31m-This command builds updated images and starts all services in the background:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-docker compose up -d --build[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-This command shuts down all the services running in the background:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-docker compose down[m
[31m-```[m
[32m+[m[32m# ResearchHub[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mA research collaboration platform focusing on regional issues, bridging academia between Central Asian and European Union universities[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## 🌍 Overview[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mThis platform bridges academia by enabling:[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Professors to post research topics, details, and student requirements[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Students to apply and schedule interviews through the platform[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rankings of universities and professors based on platform activity and engagement[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## 🚀 Features[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Professor profiles & research topic listings[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Student profiles & application system[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Interview scheduling interface[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- University & professor activity-based rankings[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- Admin interface for moderation & stats[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## 🧱 Tech Stack[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Frontend**: React, Next.js, TailwindCSS[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Backend**: Node.js (API routes), possibly integrated with a NoSQL/SQL DB[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## 📁 Folder Structure[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m├── frontend/ # Frontend source code (pages, components, styles)[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m├── backend/ # Backend routes (API handlers, DB logic, auth)[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m├── .gitignore # Ignored files and folders for Git[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m└── README.md # Project documentation[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## 📦 Usage[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mYou can build and run the entire platform using Docker Compose.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m> [!IMPORTANT][m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m> Make sure to run all Docker commands **from the root folder** of the project[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32m> (the folder containing `compose.yaml`).[m